Hi Paul,

I am not sure how OpenBugs works, I think it also uses mcmc.list data
structure when it returns the samples from the chains? Somewhere in
the output object you should probably be able to find the mcmc.list
object (you can run str() on it to find out). Then you can run
summary() on the mcmc.list object and your stats will be calculated. I
am using this for processing results from JAGS. You may need to type
"require(coda)" to run the summary().

Best wishes,

Tomas

On Tue, 16 Mar 2021 at 15:33, pjru...@ncsu.edu <pjru...@ncsu.edu> wrote:
>
> Hello:
>
> I am having some issues in fitting the Schwarz Arnason parameterization of the Jolly Seber model through data augmentation.  I am using the code provided by Royle and Dorazio in the web supplement to their book, Hierarchical Modeling and Inference in Ecology.
>
> The model is fitted to mark-recapture data on American eels Anguilla rostrata.   There are 25 encountered individuals.  To that, in the data set of capture histories, I have added 300 all-zero capture histories.   There are 34 trap sampling occasions (monthly).
>
> I have the same issue in either running the model entirely in OpenBUGS or running through R using the package R2OpenBUGS.  The model updates fine, and I can bring up trace and history plots of modeled parameters, but their are no stats provided for any modeled parameter.   With the run within OpenBUGS, I compiled 3 chains and let OpenBUGS generate initial values.   But the issue also persists when I specify initial values in R and run through R2OpenBUGS.
>
> The Royle and Dorazio model code and data list for fitting in OpenBUGS are provided below.   No data were collected for occasion number 8, which I specified as NA for each encountered individual in the data matrix.
>
> Thank you for any ideas.
> -Paul Rudershausen
